Difference Between Machine Learning and Deep Learning (Simple)

| Feature     | Machine Learning                                  | Deep Learning                                                       |
| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Meaning     | Computer learns from data using simple algorithms | Computer learns using artificial neural networks (like human brain) |
| Data Needed | Works with small or medium data                   | Needs very large data                                               |
| Human Work  | Human gives important features manually           | Learns features automatically                                       |
| Speed       | Faster to train                                   | Slower, needs powerful computers                                    |
| Accuracy    | Good for simple problems                          | Better for complex problems like images and voice                   |


====

Simple Example
1. Machine Learning Example
Problem:

Predict whether a student will pass or fail.

Input Data:
Study hours
Attendance
Internal marks
How it works:

You manually give these important details to the algorithm.

Example:
Study Hours = 8
Attendance = 90%
Internal Marks = 75

Result → Pass

Algorithms:

Decision Tree
Linear Regression
Random Forest

===========

2. Deep Learning Example
Problem:

Face Recognition in mobile phone.

Input:

A photo of your face.

How it works:

The system automatically learns:

Eyes
Nose
Face shape
Patterns

No need to manually tell features.

Example:
Input → Face Image
Output → "Phone Unlocked"

Uses:

Self-driving cars
Voice assistants
Chatbots
Image recognition
Real Life Analogy
=========


Machine Learning

Teacher gives important questions before exam.

Student studies only those questions.
======

Deep Learning

Student studies the whole book and finds important points automatically.
======

One-Line Difference

Machine Learning needs human guidance for features, while Deep Learning learns features automatically using neural networks.
